omplete.enabled=false (HTML disabled). After its only prerequisite was completed, task 4 changed to state=\\\"active\\\" with the complete toggle enabled and a \\\"1 prerequisite completed\\\" indicator.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Task 4 (one incomplete prereq) shows warning naming it: 'Prerequisite \\\"Review project proposal\\\" incomplete'. Task 7 (multiple) shows the count: \\\"2 prerequisites incomplete\\\". Both rendered as a blocked-warning observable on the card.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Task 4's complete toggle carried the disabled attribute while prerequisite \\\"Review project proposal\\\" was incomplete (click attempt timed out: \\\"element is not enabled\\\"). After completing that prerequisite, task 4 became state=\\\"active\\\" with an enabled complete toggle, i.e. eligible for completion.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Editing task 1 \\\"Review project proposal\\\", the prerequisite picker listed only: QA No Deadline, QA Alpha Task, Schedule dentist appointment, Buy groceries, Organize desk, Reply to client email. It excluded task 1 itself (self-cycle), task 4 \\\"Complete tax filing\\\" (direct: 4 depends on 1), and task 7 \\\"Submit final report\\\" (indirect: 7 depends on 4 which depends on 1). Cycle-creating tasks are unavailable as prerequisites.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"With title empty, task.form.submit enabled=false. After typing whitespace-only title \\\"   \\\", submit remained enabled=false, so no task could be created and the list stayed at 5 active.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Completing \\\"Review project proposal\\\" did not delete it — it persisted in the completed view with full details (title, priority, description, deadline) and an enabled delete button. Reopening it moved it back to the active list rather than destroying it (totals stayed at 8 tasks: 4+4 → 5+3).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Reopening a prerequisite leaves the dependent task simultaneously completed and blocked, and unrecoverable\", \"actual\": \"Completed task 4 \\\"Complete tax filing\\\" (prerequisite: task 1). Reopening task 1 was allowed with no warning or prompt. Afterwards task 4 stayed in the completed view and in the completed count (Completed 3), with complete toggle state=\\\"completed\\\" and line-through styling, while ALSO showing the blocked warning 'Prerequisite \\\"Review project proposal\\\" incomplete'. The system neither prevented the reopen nor returned task 4 to an incomplete state. Worse, task 4 is now stuck: its complete toggle (disabled=true) and edit button (disabled=true) are both disabled, so the user cannot un-complete or edit it to resolve the contradiction — only Delete remains enabled.\", \"evidence\": \"tasks.list.item.4.complete → {state:\\\"completed\\\", enabled:false}; card text ends 'Prerequisite \\\"Review project proposal\\\" incomplete'; buttons: complete disabled, edit disabled, delete enabled.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dashed SVG connectors (stroke-dasharray \\\"6,4\\\") link dependent tasks, wrapped in pointer-events-auto groups with 16px-wide hit paths. Hovering a connector at its visible segment (640,558) set the connector data-state=\\\"delayed-open\\\" and opened a tooltip: \\\"Dependency Chain / QA Alpha Task - pending / Buy groceries - pending\\\", showing the chain and each task's completion state.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Hovering tasks.list.item.7.blocked-warning (\\\"2 prerequisites incomplete\\\") opened a tooltip: \\\"Dependency Chain / Review project proposal - pending / Complete tax filing - pending\\\", identifying both still-pending prerequisites.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Cards show title + priority always (e.g. \\\"QA No Deadline / Medium\\\" with no deadline shown), plus description and deadline when supplied (\\\"QA Alpha Task / Low / Alpha description text / Sep 20\\\"). Blocking state exposed via blocked-warning ('Prerequisite \\\"Buy groceries\\\" incomplete', \\\"2 prerequisites incomplete\\\"). Completed tasks are distinguished: title computed text-decoration \\\"line-through\\\" with text-muted-foreground and bg-muted/50 card.\"}]}"
